\chapter{Lyapunov Stability and Global Convergence}

\section{Lyapunov Functionals}

Define the Lyapunov functional:
\begin{equation}
  V(\Psi)
  =
  \frac{1}{2}
  \lVert \Psi - \Psi^\ast \rVert^2,
\end{equation}
where $\Psi^\ast$ is the equilibrium state.

\section{Convergence Criteria}

Global stability requires:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{dV}{dt} < 0,
  \qquad
  \Psi \neq \Psi^\ast.
\end{equation}
This ensures monotonic convergence even under adversarial perturbation.

\section{Cross-Domain Stability}

Cross-domain stability is achieved when:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{dV_{\text{molecular}}}{dt} < 0,
  \quad
  \frac{dV_{\text{tensor}}}{dt} < 0,
  \quad
  \frac{dV_{\text{metabolic}}}{dt} < 0,
  \quad
  \frac{dV_{\text{network}}}{dt} < 0,
\end{equation}
and the combined functional satisfies:
\begin{equation}
  \frac{dV_{\text{total}}}{dt} < 0.
\end{equation}